window.docContents[203].resolve({"/Tier-2___-definitions/LibsignalBinary___Specifications___/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.LibsignalAesCbc/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___LibsignalAesCbc":{"contents":"Paper › LibsignalBinary/Specifications › LibsignalAesCbc.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the computational proof and symbolic proof 8 headline theorems depend on it 8 of 77 lines trusted trust banner B3, trusted in part source ↗Read the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\nLittle-endian byte encodings and the return helper (toLEBytes, returnToLinkRegister)Trusted in part. The headline theorems use toLEBytes, blockToBytes, and bytesToKey from this file (toLEBytes in the default library Computational/Theorems/Lemmas.lean, and blockToBytes and bytesToKey in the placed ELF headlines of Computational/Theorems/Main.lean and Symbolic/Theorems/{Refinement,Security}.lean); returnToLinkRegister is in no headline's closure under the panic-only cliExternsPlacedSig (0 external hooks). Read toLEBytes, blockToBytes, and bytesToKey. The theorems here are checked by Lean. See Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md.This file defines the little-endian conversions between BitVecs (AES blocks and keys from LibsignalBinary/Specifications/CryptoGames/AEAD/CBCDefs.lean) and byte lists, as AArch64 loads and stores them, together with returnToLinkRegister, the return to the caller that legacy fixed-image extern hooks end with. keyToBytes and the memcpy / memset hooks, used only by proofs, are in LibsignalBinary/Proofs/AesCbc/LibsignalAesCbcProofDefs.lean.Glossary: AAPCS64 = the Arm 64-bit calling convention (arguments in x0–x7, result in x0, return address in lr); LE = little-endian.returnToLinkRegister returns to lr and leaves every other register unchanged (the caller keeps nothing live in caller-saved registers across hook calls).Despite the file and namespace name, nothing here specifies AES-CBC itself: the FIPS 197 AES-256 block cipher is in LibsignalBinary/Specifications/CryptoGames/AEAD/Aes256.lean, against which the AES-256-CBC machine code is verified in LibsignalBinary/Proofs/HookDischarge/CryptoAes/ (DEV-E8).Main definitions* toLEBytes: the low n bytes of a BitVec, least significant first.* blockToBytes: the 16 LE bytes of an AES Block.* bytesToKey: the 256-bit AesKey whose LE bytes are the given list.* returnToLinkRegister: return to the caller (pc := lr).\n\n\n\nByte encodings (little-endian, as AArch64 loads and stores)\n\ndef toLEBytesL60–62 ↗#The n LE bytes of x: byte j is bits 8j .. 8j+7.\n\nabbrev blockToBytesL64–65 ↗#The 16 LE bytes of a block (inverse of bytesToBlock on 16-byte lists).\n\ndef bytesToKeyL67–69 ↗#A 256-bit key from its 32 LE bytes.\n\n1 declaration not shown (lines 73–74): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesCryptoVerification.LibsignalAesCbc.returnToLinkRegister\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"LibsignalBinary/Specifications/LibsignalAesCbc.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/LibsignalBinary___Specifications___/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.LibsignalAesCbc/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___LibsignalAesCbc"}});